+/* ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
+ * PS4: faults arrive through Sony's exception handler, not through sigaction.
+ *
+ * native_libkernel_resolve() above is bound to one PS5 libkernel build -- a
+ * 20-byte fingerprint, the module name "libkernel.sprx", an exact four-segment
+ * layout, and entry points at base+0x1600/base+0x2a0. Every one of those checks
+ * fails on PS4, so pw_native_kernel.sigaction stays NULL and the code falls
+ * back to libc sigaction. alechurri/nx-on-orbis, running on this console with
+ * this SDK, reports that faults never reach a sigaction handler here and
+ * installs sceKernelInstallExceptionHandler instead; the PS4 SDK ships a
+ * libkernel_exception.so for exactly this.
+ *
+ * ⚠ UNVERIFIED ON HARDWARE. Title GLDS10004 ("Gladius Fault Probe",
+ * src/fault-probe) answers it directly: it faults once under each mechanism and
+ * prints which one caught it. If it shows sigaction works after all, set
+ * PW_PS4_FAULTS_VIA_SONY to 0 and this whole arm drops out -- the rest of the
+ * signal path is untouched by it.
